{
 "_readme": [
  "Excel deliverables of the `requirements` method (English). D1 = source inventory and epic structure, D2 = the requirement set with traceability.",
  "Every aggregate is a formula over the detail sheets. The engine adds an Open_Questions sheet whenever client questions exist.",
  "Formula placeholders: {r} {MAXR} {rng:Sheet.col_id} {col:id} {cell:id} {L:token} {p:param} {row} {x:key}."
 ],
 "deliverables": {
  "D1": {
   "title": "D1 Source inventory and epic structure",
   "requires": [
    "inventory"
   ],
   "purpose": "Which of the client's documents, board exports and workshop results this requirement set is built on, what each of them is worth as a base (extraction quality, citable anchors), and the epic structure the requirements are organised in - with the expected number of requirements per epic.",
   "sources": "corpus/index.json (indexed client material with stable locators), corpus/unextractable.md, analysis/inventory/source_inventory.md",
   "extra": "Every source carries the id it is cited by (SRC-nnn). A requirement in D2 points at an anchor of one of these sources; a source listed as `unextractable` can only ever be cited as `visual, unverified`, which is why its topics appear as questions to the client rather than as requirements.",
   "sheets": [
    {
     "name": "Management_Summary",
     "type": "mgmt",
     "readme": "KPIs (formulas over the detail sheets) and the assessment of the source base",
     "kpis": [
      {
       "label": "Sources indexed",
       "formula": "=COUNTA({rng:Sources.id})",
       "note": "documents, presentations, spreadsheets and board exports the requirement set is built on (sheet Sources)"
      },
      {
       "label": "of which fully readable",
       "formula": "=COUNTIF({rng:Sources.index_quality},\"good\")",
       "note": "text could be extracted completely, so every statement about them is checkable at an anchor"
      },
      {
       "label": "of which partially readable",
       "formula": "=COUNTIF({rng:Sources.index_quality},\"partial*\")+COUNTIF({rng:Sources.index_quality},\"none*\")",
       "note": "image-heavy slides or scans without a text layer - statements about them stay `visual, unverified`"
      },
      {
       "label": "of which not readable at all",
       "formula": "=COUNTIF({rng:Sources.index_quality},\"unextractable\")",
       "note": "images and diagrams without text: their topics become questions to the client, never inferred requirements"
      },
      {
       "label": "Citable anchors",
       "formula": "=SUM({rng:Sources.anchors})",
       "note": "pages, slides, paragraph blocks, spreadsheet rows and board items a requirement can point at"
      },
      {
       "label": "{unit.noun_plural}",
       "formula": "=COUNTA({rng:Epics.name})",
       "note": "the structure the requirements are organised in (sheet {unit.noun_plural})"
      },
      {
       "label": "of which functional",
       "formula": "=COUNTIF({rng:Epics.kind},\"{L:functional}\")",
       "note": "what the business can do with the {system.type}"
      },
      {
       "label": "of which technical",
       "formula": "=COUNTIF({rng:Epics.kind},\"{L:technical}\")",
       "note": "interfaces to other systems, platform, data, migration"
      },
      {
       "label": "of which non-functional",
       "formula": "=COUNTIF({rng:Epics.kind},\"{L:nfr}\")",
       "note": "measurable qualities: performance, availability, security, accessibility, operability"
      },
      {
       "label": "Requirements expected",
       "formula": "=SUM({rng:Epics.estimated_requirements})",
       "note": "estimate per epic from the source passages that carry it - the figure D2 is measured against"
      },
      {
       "label": "{unit.noun_plural} out of scope",
       "formula": "=COUNTIF({rng:Epics.activation},\"{L:out-of-scope}\")",
       "note": "topics the client's material explicitly excludes - listed so nobody has to ask twice"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "README",
     "type": "readme"
    },
    {
     "name": "Sources",
     "type": "table",
     "dataset": "sources",
     "row_key": "id",
     "readme": "One row per indexed source: what it is, what it covers, how well it can be cited",
     "columns": [
      {
       "header": "Source",
       "field": "id",
       "width": 11
      },
      {
